    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey`, keeping structural impact low by adding small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods.\n\n**New files (each a small, self-contained unit):**\n- `IdentityKey.java` \u2014 the single source of truth: `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`. `forRequest(...)` computes a new owner's would-be key (deriving its household id the same way `AssignHousehold` does, so a genuine full-key collision is caught); `forOwner(...)` computes an existing owner's key. Both normalize telephone via `E164` and lowercase email so requests and stored rows compare uniformly.\n- `RejectDuplicateIdentity.java` \u2014 one step that scans existing owners and throws 409 only on a whole-key match.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` + its handler + escalation YAML \u2014 mirrors the existing 409 pattern.\n\n**Edits (minimal):**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced the three separate `rejectDuplicateTelephone/Email/Household` steps with the single `rejectDuplicateIdentity` step.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema (so the response returns it).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one `@Mapping` expression delegating to `IdentityKey.forOwner(owner)`, following the existing derived-field convention (so both POST and GET responses carry it).\n\n**Behaviour change, as specified:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now have different `identityKey`s and are both accepted \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The old per-field reject classes are left unwired (inert) rather than deleted, avoiding touching ~12 extra files.\n\nThe one existing/new acceptance test (`coreRejectsIdentityCollision` \u2014 same telephone \u21d2 409) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
